{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/style/contrast","title":"Text contrast, proven without a browser","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"text-contrast-proven-without-a-browser","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Text contrast, proven without a browser"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"npm run style:check"},{"t":"text","text":" reads your sheets and your templates and answers one"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"question, for every element it can prove holds text, in every state your axes"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"can produce:"}]},{"t":"quote","children":[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"is this text readable on the background it is actually painted on?"}]}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"It is WCAG 2.2 §1.4.3 level AA — "},{"t":"code","text":"4.5:1"},{"t":"text","text":" for normal text, "},{"t":"code","text":"3:1"},{"t":"text","text":" for large text"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"— and it needs no browser, no screenshot and no Playwright run."}]},{"t":"callout","tone":"warning","caption":"What this is not","children":[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"This proves "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"text contrast"}]},{"t":"text","text":", in a declared subset of CSS. It is not an"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"accessibility audit, and a green run is not a claim that your application is"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"accessible. Focus order, names, roles, motion, target size and everything else"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"are elsewhere. Read "},{"t":"link","href":"#the-coverage-contract","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"the coverage contract"}]},{"t":"text","text":" before you"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"put a badge on it."}]}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"running-it","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Running it"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"npm","kind":"function"},{"text":" "},{"text":"run","kind":"string"},{"text":" "},{"text":"style:check","kind":"string"}]}],"filename":"","language":"bash","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"In a project generated with typed CSS this is already wired: it builds once so"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the style plugin writes "},{"t":"code","text":".craft/style-graph.json"},{"t":"text","text":", then analyses that dump"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"together with your TypeScript program."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"By hand, on an existing project:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"npx","kind":"function"},{"text":" "},{"text":"craft-graph","kind":"string"},{"text":" "},{"text":"--style-contrast","kind":"string"},{"text":" "},{"text":"--style-dump","kind":"string"},{"text":" "},{"text":".craft/style-graph.json","kind":"string"},{"text":" "},{"text":"--project","kind":"string"},{"text":" "},{"text":"tsconfig.app.json","kind":"string"}]}],"filename":"","language":"bash","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"--json"},{"t":"text","text":" gives a stable machine-readable report for CI. Two runs on unchanged"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"sources produce byte-identical output."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Unlike "},{"t":"code","text":"--style-matrix"},{"t":"text","text":" and "},{"t":"code","text":"--style-debt"},{"t":"text","text":", this command "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"does"}]},{"t":"text","text":" build the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"TypeScript program. It has to: a contrast proof needs to know which element"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"carries which class and what sits above it, and no style dump has ever seen a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"template."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"reading-a-failure","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Reading a failure"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"contrast/fail"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"route: /checkout"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"component: SubmitButton"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"element: button.root"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"scenario: interaction.hover=active+tone=warning"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"foreground: ui.text.onAccent #ffffff (dsButton-root → --dsButton-ink (initial))"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"background: ui.accent.warning.dark #f5b544 (button.root: dsButton-root → --dsButton-bg)"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"font: 14px / 600 (normal text)"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"ratio: 1.81:1"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"required: 4.5:1"}]}],"filename":"","language":"","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Every line is there because a report missing it sends you to the wrong file:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"scenario"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — the exact combination. Not \"the warning button\": the warning"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"button "},{"t":"em","children":[{"t":"text","text":"under the pointer"}]},{"t":"text","text":", which is often the only failing one."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"foreground / background"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — the token name first, then the value, then the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"chain that produced it. "},{"t":"code","text":"ui.accent.warning.dark"},{"t":"text","text":" tells you which token to"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"change; "},{"t":"code","text":"dsButton-root → --dsButton-bg"},{"t":"text","text":" tells you which rule put it there."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"font"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — with the threshold it earned. See"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"link","href":"#which-threshold-applies","external":false,"children":[{"t":"text","text":"large text"}]},{"t":"text","text":"."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Rows that resolve to the same answer are folded together and list the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"scenarios they stand for under "},{"t":"code","text":"also in:"},{"t":"text","text":", so a five-tone button does not"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"print five identical lines."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"the-two-halves-and-why-only-one-of-them-fails-a-build","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The two halves, and why only one of them fails a build"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[],[{"t":"code","text":"--palette-contrast"}],[{"t":"code","text":"--style-contrast"}]],"rows":[[[{"t":"text","text":"reads"}],[{"t":"text","text":"the dump alone"}],[{"t":"text","text":"the dump "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"and"}]},{"t":"text","text":" the templates"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"answers"}],[{"t":"text","text":"every pair your palette can express"}],[{"t":"text","text":"every pair an element is actually painted in"}]],[[{"t":"text","text":"verdict"}],[{"t":"text","text":"informative"}],[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"blocking"}]},{"t":"text","text":""}]]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A palette of twenty tokens has hundreds of pairs and an application renders a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"few dozen of them. Failing a build on "},{"t":"code","text":"ui.text.onAccent"},{"t":"text","text":" over"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"ui.surface.page"},{"t":"text","text":" — white on white, and a combination no element uses — trains"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"people to switch the check off, and takes the real failures with it."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"So the matrix is a table you read while designing, and the analysis is the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"gate. When you pass the analysis's results to "},{"t":"code","text":"paletteContrastMatrix"},{"t":"text","text":", each"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"pair also gets a "},{"t":"code","text":"usedBy"},{"t":"text","text":" list of the elements that render it; without them the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"field is "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"absent"}]},{"t":"text","text":" rather than empty, because \"nobody looked\" and \"the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"analysis looked and found nowhere\" are different answers."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"which-threshold-applies","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Which threshold applies"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"large if "},{"t":"code","text":"font-size >= 24px"},{"t":"text","text":";"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"large if "},{"t":"code","text":"font-size >= 18.5px"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"and"}]},{"t":"text","text":" the weight is at least "},{"t":"code","text":"700"},{"t":"text","text":";"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"normal otherwise."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Two consequences worth knowing before you argue with a report:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"text.lg"},{"t":"text","text":" is "},{"t":"code","text":"1.125rem"},{"t":"text","text":" — "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"18px"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — so a bold title at that size is "},{"t":"em","children":[{"t":"text","text":"normal"}]},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"text and needs "},{"t":"code","text":"4.5:1"},{"t":"text","text":". It misses the large threshold by half a pixel."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"600"},{"t":"text","text":" is not bold. WCAG says \"bold\" without a number and CSS says bold is"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"700; reading "},{"t":"code","text":"600"},{"t":"text","text":" as bold would lower a threshold on an ambiguity, which is"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the wrong side to err on."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"rem"},{"t":"text","text":" becomes pixels against a 16px root. If your page sets a different root"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"size outside CraftTS, say so — nothing in the dump can know."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The ratio is "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"never rounded before it is compared"}]},{"t":"text","text":". "},{"t":"code","text":"4.4999:1"},{"t":"text","text":" fails a 4.5"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"threshold, even though the report prints it as "},{"t":"code","text":"4.49:1"},{"t":"text","text":"."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"how-colour-is-resolved","children":[{"t":"text","text":"How colour is resolved"}]},{"t":"heading","level":3,"id":"color-is-inherited","children":[{"t":"code","text":"color"},{"t":"text","text":" is inherited"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The analysis walks the element's ancestor chain outside-in, exactly as the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"cascade does. A paragraph that sets no colour of its own takes the one from"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"its card, or from the theme wrapper above it."}]},{"t":"heading","level":3,"id":"the-background-is-the-first-opaque-thing-underneath","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The background is the first opaque thing underneath"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Starting at the element and walking outwards:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"an element that paints nothing is transparent, and the search continues;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"the first opaque colour wins;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"an element that paints something the model cannot read — an image, a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"semi-transparent fill, anything behind an "},{"t":"code","text":"opacity"},{"t":"text","text":" — "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"stops"}]},{"t":"text","text":" the search"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"and produces "},{"t":"code","text":"indeterminate"},{"t":"text","text":", because whatever is behind it is no longer"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"what the text is composited against."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"If nothing in the chain paints, that is "},{"t":"code","text":"unknown-background"},{"t":"text","text":". It is not"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"\"assume white\": a white assumption is right on one theme and wrong on the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"other."}]},{"t":"heading","level":3,"id":"variables-resolve-the-way-property-says-they-do","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Variables resolve the way "},{"t":"code","text":"@property"},{"t":"text","text":" says they do"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"a registered variable nobody wrote resolves to its "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"registered initial"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"value"}]},{"t":"text","text":", not to the "},{"t":"code","text":"var()"},{"t":"text","text":" fallback;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"inherits: false"},{"t":"text","text":" really does not cross into a child — a theme variable set"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"on a wrapper reaches the button, a component variable does not."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"That last one is the trap the design system is full of, and getting it wrong"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"would prove the wrong colour for every component under a themed wrapper."}]},{"t":"heading","level":3,"id":"the-cascade-is-replayed-not-approximated","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The cascade is replayed, not approximated"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Three tie-breaks, in the browser's order:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Layer."}]},{"t":"text","text":" Unconditional atoms land in "},{"t":"code","text":"components"},{"t":"text","text":", conditional ones in"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"variants"},{"t":"text","text":", so every variant beats every base rule."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Specificity"}]},{"t":"text","text":", inside "},{"t":"code","text":"variants"},{"t":"text","text":". "},{"t":"code","text":"&[data-tone='warning']:hover"},{"t":"text","text":" has one"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"more selector fragment than "},{"t":"code","text":"&[data-tone='warning']"},{"t":"text","text":", so the hovered fill"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"wins — whatever the source order. A media query contributes nothing."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Source order"}]},{"t":"text","text":", last, which is atomic class-name order because that is"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"how the emitter sorts the layer."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Getting the second wrong is the interesting failure: a solver would resolve a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"tone-plus-hover button to its resting fill and report "},{"t":"code","text":"pass"},{"t":"text","text":" on the state that"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"fails."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"hover-is-an-axis","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Hover is an axis"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"when","kind":"function"},{"text":"(tone.warning, [","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  "},{"text":"set","kind":"function"},{"text":"(buttonVars.bg, ui.accent.warning),","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  "},{"text":"when","kind":"function"},{"text":"(interaction.hover, [","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"set","kind":"function"},{"text":"(buttonVars.bg, ui.accent.warningHover)]),","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"]);","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"interaction.hover"},{"t":"text","text":" emits the same "},{"t":"code","text":":hover"},{"t":"text","text":" rule a hand-written selector would."},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"What it adds is that the point lands in the class's variant contract — so the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"visual matrix captures the hovered state, and this analysis crosses the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"colours it writes with the text that sits on them."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A "},{"t":"code","text":":hover"},{"t":"text","text":" typed into a string is invisible to both. That is how a button ends"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"up readable at rest and unreadable under the pointer: the one state nobody"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"screenshots. The "},{"t":"code","text":"prefer-hover-axis"},{"t":"text","text":" lint rule refuses it."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The axis carries its own driver ("},{"t":"code","text":"{ kind: 'selfState', state: 'hover' }"},{"t":"text","text":"), so a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"capture of the hovered state is something a harness can actually produce."},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"applyScenario"},{"t":"text","text":" asks the page to move a real pointer and throws if it cannot —"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"dispatching a "},{"t":"code","text":"mouseover"},{"t":"text","text":" event would fire listeners and leave the pseudo-class"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"untouched, producing a screenshot of the base state that passes forever."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The cost is real and it is a decision: hover doubled the demo button's matrix"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"from 18 scenarios to 36. That is why the axis has to be in the sheet's budget."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"naming-your-palette","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Naming your palette"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"export","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"const","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"ui"},{"text":" "},{"text":"=","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"definePalette","kind":"function"},{"text":"(","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'ui'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":", {","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  text: { onAccent: { light: ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'#ffffff'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":", dark: ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'#0b0d11'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":" } },","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"  accent: { warning: { light: ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'#8a5a00'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":", dark: ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"'#f5b544'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":" } },","kind":"punctuation"}]},{"tokens":[{"text":"});","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"ts","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The name travels with every colour, through variables and "},{"t":"code","text":"darkOf()"},{"t":"text","text":", all the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"way into the report. "},{"t":"code","text":"definePalette(spec)"},{"t":"text","text":" without a name still works and still"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"carries the group and the token — you get "},{"t":"code","text":"(unnamed).accent.warning"},{"t":"text","text":", which"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"points at the right entry and asks to be named."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Write hovered and pressed fills as "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"tokens"}]},{"t":"text","text":", not as a "},{"t":"code","text":"darken()"},{"t":"text","text":" at the use"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"site. A function hides the resulting colour from the palette, and the palette"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"is where the contrast question gets settled once instead of per component."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"the-coverage-contract","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The coverage contract"}]},{"t":"heading","level":3,"id":"covered-in-v1","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Covered in v1"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"opaque colours in hexadecimal or "},{"t":"code","text":"rgb()"},{"t":"text","text":"/"},{"t":"code","text":"rgba()"},{"t":"text","text":";"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"inherited "},{"t":"code","text":"color"},{"t":"text","text":";"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"code","text":"background-color"},{"t":"text","text":", local or seen through transparent ancestors;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"CraftTS variables declared with "},{"t":"code","text":"cssVars()"},{"t":"text","text":", their initial values, their"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"conditional writes and their "},{"t":"code","text":"var()"},{"t":"text","text":" fallbacks;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"constant classes from "},{"t":"code","text":"craftStyles()"},{"t":"text","text":";"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"light and dark themes;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"every finite state and size axis, "},{"t":"code","text":"interaction.hover"},{"t":"text","text":" included;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"static and dynamic text, wherever the element can be proven to hold text;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"a component evaluated once per surface it is rendered on."}]}]]},{"t":"heading","level":3,"id":"seen-but-not-solvable-in-v1","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Seen but not solvable in v1"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"When one of these constructs reaches the graph, it produces "},{"t":"code","text":"indeterminate"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"with its reason — never a pass:"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"images and gradients recorded as "},{"t":"code","text":"background-image"},{"t":"text","text":";"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"an "},{"t":"code","text":"opacity"},{"t":"text","text":" below 1 on the text or an element behind it;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"semi-transparent colours, which would need compositing;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"a dynamic class the template graph cannot resolve;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"an unknown foreground, background or font size;"}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"a scenario or render context that exceeds the configured analysis limit."}]}]]},{"t":"heading","level":3,"id":"outside-the-observable-boundary","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Outside the observable boundary"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"External stylesheets, inline styles outside CraftTS, "},{"t":"code","text":"canvas"},{"t":"text","text":", text inside SVG,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"generated pseudo-element content, filters and blend modes do not necessarily"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"enter the typed style dump. The analyser cannot emit an "},{"t":"code","text":"indeterminate"},{"t":"text","text":" for a"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"declaration it never receives. The "},{"t":"code","text":"typedCss"},{"t":"text","text":" ESLint preset refuses hand-written"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":":hover"},{"t":"text","text":", but this is not a general CSS crawler."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The large-text threshold is calculated from CSS pixels and weight. The analyser"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"does not inspect the script, font face or cap height, so it does not detect CJK"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"or unusual font geometry and does not emit a CJK-specific diagnostic. Treat"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"those surfaces as outside the v1 proof unless their typography convention has"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"been validated separately."}]},{"t":"heading","level":3,"id":"what-indeterminate-means-and-why-it-fails-by-default","children":[{"t":"text","text":"What "},{"t":"code","text":"indeterminate"},{"t":"text","text":" means, and why it fails by default"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"t":"text","text":"reason"}],[{"t":"text","text":"what happened"}]],"rows":[[[{"t":"code","text":"unknown-foreground"}],[{"t":"text","text":"nothing readable sets the text colour"}]],[[{"t":"code","text":"unknown-background"}],[{"t":"text","text":"nothing in the chain paints an opaque surface"}]],[[{"t":"code","text":"unknown-font-size"}],[{"t":"text","text":"the size is not a length this can turn into pixels"}]],[[{"t":"code","text":"unsupported-background"}],[{"t":"text","text":"an image, a gradient, a blend, or an alpha"}]],[[{"t":"code","text":"dynamic-style"}],[{"t":"text","text":"the class is assembled at runtime"}]],[[{"t":"code","text":"incomplete-render-context"}],[{"t":"text","text":"the component is rendered somewhere unanalysed"}]]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Indeterminate results fail the run."}]},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"--allow-indeterminate"},{"t":"text","text":" downgrades them"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"to warnings, and you have to type it. A check whose default treats \"I could not"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"tell\" as \"fine\" reports a clean bill on the half of the application it"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"understood — and that half is exactly where the gradients and the runtime"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"colours live."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A report with "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"no violations and open indeterminates is not a proof."}]},{"t":"text","text":" The"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"summary prints all three counts for that reason:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"Text contrast: 41 pass, 0 fail, 3 indeterminate (44 checked)."}]}],"filename":"","language":"","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Zero checked fails even with "},{"t":"code","text":"--allow-indeterminate"},{"t":"text","text":": it nearly always means"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the dump and the program describe different applications, and there is no"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"result to review or waive."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"fixing-a-violation","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Fixing a violation"}]},{"t":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Read the scenario."}]},{"t":"text","text":" If only the hovered or only the dark row fails, the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"fix belongs to that one rule, not to the token everything uses."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Read the token names."}]},{"t":"text","text":" A pair that fails in several places is a palette"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"decision — change the token once, and "},{"t":"code","text":"usedBy"},{"t":"text","text":" tells you what moves."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Change the token, not the call site."}]},{"t":"text","text":" A local override is a colour the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"palette no longer describes, and the next component repeats the bug."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"If the text is genuinely large"}]},{"t":"text","text":", check that the sheet says so. 18px bold"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"is normal text; 22px bold is large."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Re-run."}]},{"t":"text","text":" The report is deterministic, so a diff of two JSON runs shows"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"exactly what your change moved."}]}]]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"clearing-an-indeterminate","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Clearing an indeterminate"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"You have two honest moves, and inventing a colour is not one of them."}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Bring the surface into the model."}]},{"t":"text","text":" A "},{"t":"code","text":"background-color"},{"t":"text","text":" set in raw CSS is"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"the common case."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Give the text a surface it can be measured against."}]},{"t":"text","text":" Text over a hero"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"image has no ratio because it has no single background — put it on a panel,"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"or accept that it cannot be proven."}]}]]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"If a surface lives entirely outside the observable graph, it will not create an"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"indeterminate to clear. Keep that exclusion visible in review and do not"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"describe the strict check as covering it."}]},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"migrating-an-existing-project","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Migrating an existing project"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"You do not need to recreate the application or add Playwright. Align the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"installed "},{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/*"},{"t":"text","text":" packages on the same current version; the contrast CLI"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"is provided by "},{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/dev-tools"},{"t":"text","text":", while "},{"t":"code","text":"@craft-ts/style-testing"},{"t":"text","text":" is only"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"needed for visual scenarios and attestation."}]},{"t":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Name each palette: "},{"t":"code","text":"definePalette('ui', spec)"},{"t":"text","text":". Nothing else changes."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Turn hand-written "},{"t":"code","text":":hover"},{"t":"text","text":" rules into "},{"t":"code","text":"when(interaction.hover, …)"},{"t":"text","text":" and add"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"interaction"},{"t":"text","text":" to those sheets' budgets. "},{"t":"code","text":"prefer-hover-axis"},{"t":"text","text":" finds them."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Enable "},{"t":"code","text":"craftRules.configs.typedCss.rules"},{"t":"text","text":" in ESLint. It refuses the raw hover"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"that the analysis would otherwise not see."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Add "},{"t":"code","text":"dumpPath: '.craft/style-graph.json'"},{"t":"text","text":" to "},{"t":"code","text":"craftStyle()"},{"t":"text","text":" in"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"code","text":"vite.config.ts"},{"t":"text","text":" and keep "},{"t":"code","text":"virtual:craft-style.css"},{"t":"text","text":" imported at app entry."}]}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Make "},{"t":"code","text":"style:check"},{"t":"text","text":" build the app, then run the strict analysis:"}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"craft-graph","kind":"function"},{"text":" "},{"text":"--style-contrast","kind":"string"},{"text":" "},{"text":"--style-dump","kind":"string"},{"text":" "},{"text":".craft/style-graph.json","kind":"string"},{"text":" "},{"text":"--project","kind":"string"},{"text":" "},{"text":"tsconfig.app.json","kind":"string"}]}],"filename":"","language":"bash","numbered":false,"firstLine":1}],[{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Run that command with "},{"t":"code","text":"--allow-indeterminate"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"once"}]},{"t":"text","text":", to inventory the"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"visible gaps. Close them and remove the flag before making the check a CI"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"gate. A lint "},{"t":"code","text":"uncovered"},{"t":"text","text":" exemption remains outside the proof."}]}]]}],"outline":[{"level":2,"id":"running-it","text":"Running it"},{"level":2,"id":"reading-a-failure","text":"Reading a failure"},{"level":2,"id":"the-two-halves-and-why-only-one-of-them-fails-a-build","text":"The two halves, and why only one of them fails a build"},{"level":2,"id":"which-threshold-applies","text":"Which threshold applies"},{"level":2,"id":"how-colour-is-resolved","text":"How colour is resolved"},{"level":3,"id":"color-is-inherited","text":"color is inherited"},{"level":3,"id":"the-background-is-the-first-opaque-thing-underneath","text":"The background is the first opaque thing underneath"},{"level":3,"id":"variables-resolve-the-way-property-says-they-do","text":"Variables resolve the way @property says they do"},{"level":3,"id":"the-cascade-is-replayed-not-approximated","text":"The cascade is replayed, not approximated"},{"level":2,"id":"hover-is-an-axis","text":"Hover is an axis"},{"level":2,"id":"naming-your-palette","text":"Naming your palette"},{"level":2,"id":"the-coverage-contract","text":"The coverage contract"},{"level":3,"id":"covered-in-v1","text":"Covered in v1"},{"level":3,"id":"seen-but-not-solvable-in-v1","text":"Seen but not solvable in v1"},{"level":3,"id":"outside-the-observable-boundary","text":"Outside the observable boundary"},{"level":3,"id":"what-indeterminate-means-and-why-it-fails-by-default","text":"What indeterminate means, and why it fails by default"},{"level":2,"id":"fixing-a-violation","text":"Fixing a violation"},{"level":2,"id":"clearing-an-indeterminate","text":"Clearing an indeterminate"},{"level":2,"id":"migrating-an-existing-project","text":"Migrating an existing project"}]}